# ===========================================================================
#  Sizzle (local-GPU edition) - what does and does not go into the backup repo.
#
#  Guiding rule: commit everything needed to REBUILD this project on a
#  different GPU box. Exclude only (a) things that are enormous and
#  re-downloadable, (b) things that are clones of other repos, (c) things that
#  are specific to one machine, and (d) runtime scratch.
#
#  Every exclusion below has a documented way to recreate it. See SETUP.md.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Rebuilt by install.bat / install.sh. requirements.txt + requirements.lock.txt
# are committed, so the environment is reproducible without the venv itself.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Local model weights (~123 GB) ----------------------------------------
# THE big one. Six safetensors files plus the Gemma 3 12B text encoder.
# Re-fetch with: python scripts/download_models.py
# Full instructions (including the gated Gemma repo): models/README.md
# (git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so exclude the CONTENTS
# with models/* - with "models/" the negation below would never fire.)
models/*
!models/README.md

# --- Vendored upstream checkouts ------------------------------------------
# Both of these are git clones of OTHER repositories. Committing them would
# nest a repo inside this one, and neither is ours to redistribute.
#
#   LTX-2/          Lightricks' inference pipelines. install.bat/.sh clones it.
#                   Exact commit this build was validated against is pinned in
#                   VENDOR-PINS.txt - use it if HEAD ever breaks.
#   Sizzle_upstream/  Read-only reference copy of the original hosted-render
#                   Sizzle (github.com/hughesdo/Sizzle), kept side-by-side to
#                   diff against. Not needed to run anything.
LTX-2/
Sizzle_upstream/

# --- Machine-local TLS bundle ---------------------------------------------
# certs/ca-bundle.pem embeds this box's antivirus MITM root. It is not a secret
# (no private keys) but it is machine-specific and WRONG on any other host.
# The app falls back to certifi when it is absent. Regenerate on the new box
# only if you actually hit CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED: scripts/fix-certs.ps1
certs/ca-bundle.pem

# --- Runtime artifacts (uploads, clips, renders, logs, usage ledger) ------
# Recreated on demand; config.ensure_dirs() makes the tree at startup.
_work/*
!_work/README.md
*.log
*.log.*

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: `.env` IS COMMITTED in this backup, deliberately - it carries the
# render settings this build was tuned with and records that the Gemma license
# was accepted. It was audited before the first commit and contains NO
# credentials (its only active line is SIZZLE_BACKEND=local).
#
# ==> Put anything secret in `.env.local` instead, which stays ignored. <==
#     backend/config.py reads .env; to point it elsewhere set SIZZLE_ENV_FILE.
#     Real keys to keep OUT of .env: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, HF_TOKEN.
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key
!certs/*.md

# --- Personal working notes / planning docs (kept local, not published) ---
notes.txt
PLAN.md
BUILD-TRACKER.md
IMPROVEMENT-PLAN.md
yolo.bat

# --- Working screenshots dropped in the repo root --------------------------
/*.png

# --- Editor / OS junk ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
